1
00:00:01,552 --> 00:00:04,681
Goodbye, Buffalo Crush!

2
00:00:06,551 --> 00:00:10,704
What's the speed of a car that takes 8 hours to travel 456 km?

3
00:00:10,704 --> 00:00:12,644
57 kilometers per hour.

4
00:00:12,644 --> 00:00:13,775
Hehehe...

5
00:00:13,775 --> 00:00:17,466
How far does a plane flying at 340 meters per second travel over seven seconds?

6
00:00:17,466 --> 00:00:18,902
2,380 meters.

7
00:00:18,902 --> 00:00:20,219
Hehehe!

8
00:00:20,219 --> 00:00:21,870
Homework done!

9
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:26,245
Jun. It's no use knowing the answers if you don't know how to solve the problems.

10
00:00:26,245 --> 00:00:27,719
But you know time is money!

11
00:00:27,719 --> 00:00:31,948
I'd really like to save time on doing homework so I can read more!

12
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,475
But... that's a comic book.

13
00:00:33,475 --> 00:00:35,176
A comic book is still a book!

14
00:00:35,176 --> 00:00:36,484
That's true.

15
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:39,133
Tell me. Would you like to read some of my comics sometime?

16
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:40,895
Aagh!

17
00:00:40,895 --> 00:00:43,655
Dad! I told you to knock first!

18
00:00:43,655 --> 00:00:44,811
I did.

19
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:46,756
But... who were you talking to?

20
00:00:46,756 --> 00:00:49,554
Uh, haha... I was just talking to myself.

21
00:00:49,554 --> 00:00:52,917
Talking to yourself means that you are under a lot of stress.

22
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:55,128
You should know the Milky Way will be closed tomorrow.

23
00:00:55,128 --> 00:00:56,527
So how about we go on a family road trip?

24
00:00:56,527 --> 00:00:58,326
Yahoo! I'd love to!

25
00:01:06,549 --> 00:01:08,864
Why does it feel as though things aren't going our way?

26
00:01:08,864 --> 00:01:12,989
Can't you come up with some brilliant plan to steal the treasure of planet Machina?!

27
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,798
We already know where it is...

28
00:01:14,798 --> 00:01:16,668
So why not launch a surprise attack?!

29
00:01:16,668 --> 00:01:18,289
A surprise attack?

30
00:01:18,289 --> 00:01:21,567
Yes! Or we could try taking the child's family hostage!

31
00:01:21,567 --> 00:01:23,269
We only here for treasure.

32
00:01:23,269 --> 00:01:25,611
Leave uninvolved humans out of this.

33
00:01:25,611 --> 00:01:29,561
Hahaha! I see you have some loyalty in you!

34
00:01:29,561 --> 00:01:33,518
If you have a better idea, why not share it with us, Buffalo Crush?

35
00:01:33,518 --> 00:01:34,834
Me handle this.

36
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:37,408
Where are you off to now?!

37
00:01:37,408 --> 00:01:38,194
Let him go!

38
00:01:38,194 --> 00:01:41,401
A pirate always stays true to his word!

39
00:01:41,609 --> 00:01:45,387
Me don't want her to get hurt.

40
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,384
Ugh... what's so fun about going on a road trip?

41
00:01:57,384 --> 00:01:59,310
Shh! Be quiet!

42
00:01:59,310 --> 00:02:01,272
I could get there way faster than a car!

43
00:02:01,272 --> 00:02:02,552
Shhh!

44
00:02:02,552 --> 00:02:04,152
Talking to yourself again?

45
00:02:04,152 --> 00:02:06,575
Ahahaha! It's nothing!

46
00:02:06,575 --> 00:02:08,776
He's starting to take after you.

47
00:02:08,776 --> 00:02:09,914
Me?

48
00:02:09,914 --> 00:02:12,376
You always do that when you're driving, haven't you noticed?

49
00:02:12,376 --> 00:02:13,615
Ha, do I really?

50
00:02:14,711 --> 00:02:20,142
What's the hurry?! You gotta go to the bathroom?! Why didn't you go earlier?! You're a terrible driver! What if something had happened?!

51
00:02:20,142 --> 00:02:22,573
-See?
-So irresponsible!

52
00:02:23,877 --> 00:02:26,550
Uh... excuse me?

53
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:29,256
Ooh, what a strange car!

54
00:02:29,703 --> 00:02:31,740
Do you need something from them?

55
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,610
Uh, yeah...

56
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:35,429
I heard they're not home today.

57
00:02:35,429 --> 00:02:38,521
They were all going on a trip to the Itar Plateau.

58
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:40,848
Itar... Plateau?

59
00:02:40,848 --> 00:02:41,706
Thank you.

60
00:02:41,706 --> 00:02:42,692
Itar Plateau, Itar Plateau...

61
00:02:44,978 --> 00:02:46,277
They're in trouble!

62
00:02:47,712 --> 00:02:51,562
Your call could not be connected. Please try again later.

63
00:02:55,146 --> 00:02:56,496
Ugh! I'm bored!

64
00:02:56,496 --> 00:02:59,305
If I knew it would be like this, I would've stayed home!

65
00:02:59,741 --> 00:03:00,652
Jun.

66
00:03:00,652 --> 00:03:01,467
Yeah?

67
00:03:01,467 --> 00:03:03,758
Do you have... anything you want to tell me?

68
00:03:03,758 --> 00:03:05,877
Uh... something to tell you, like...

69
00:03:05,877 --> 00:03:09,203
Maybe something like any worries or secrets you may have.

70
00:03:09,203 --> 00:03:11,780
You know, you can always tell me anything.

71
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:13,271
Uhh... haha...

72
00:03:13,271 --> 00:03:15,865
Dad! I don't have any secrets.

73
00:03:15,865 --> 00:03:18,400
Jun. Do you think we've been discovered?

74
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,545
There's no way.

75
00:03:22,913 --> 00:03:25,259
I gotta use the restroom first. You guys go ahead.

76
00:03:25,259 --> 00:03:26,300
Okay!

77
00:03:26,389 --> 00:03:28,734
Woah! Haha!

78
00:03:29,789 --> 00:03:31,919
How's the view? Glad you came?

79
00:03:31,919 --> 00:03:33,170
Yeah!

80
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:35,438
I used to have worries at your age, too.

81
00:03:35,438 --> 00:03:37,364
When I couldn't work things out,

82
00:03:37,364 --> 00:03:41,149
-I would turn to nature to forget about them all.
-Where is this conversation going?

83
00:03:41,149 --> 00:03:43,942
You're 12 and there are things you don't want to tell us.

84
00:03:43,942 --> 00:03:47,355
But it's not right to tell lies. That would make your parents sad.

85
00:03:47,355 --> 00:03:50,877
I-I would never lie to you guys, you know that.

86
00:03:50,877 --> 00:03:52,143
Just a second.

87
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:55,170
Hello? Theo?

88
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:56,447
Jun! Bad news!

89
00:03:56,447 --> 00:03:58,918
Buffalo Crush was at your place!

90
00:03:58,918 --> 00:04:00,299
What?! Again?!

91
00:04:00,299 --> 00:04:02,506
I think he's headed your way!

92
00:04:09,115 --> 00:04:10,568
Huh? What's wrong?

93
00:04:11,955 --> 00:04:13,848
Huh? Huh!

94
00:04:15,574 --> 00:04:13,411
Hey, Jun!

95
00:04:16,411 --> 00:04:17,177
Mom!

96
00:04:17,348 --> 00:04:18,264
Jun!

97
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:23,230
Found you! Yaah!

98
00:04:23,230 --> 00:04:24,324
Huh?

99
00:04:25,285 --> 00:04:28,800
Please give back Machina's treasure!

100
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,300
You are... what treasure?

101
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:34,153
Your son have it. I beg you! Please!

102
00:04:34,153 --> 00:04:35,718
Me owe miss Yuri my life!

103
00:04:35,718 --> 00:04:38,137
Me don't want you getting hurt over this.

104
00:04:38,802 --> 00:04:39,480
Mom!

105
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,146
Darling, what's going on?!

106
00:04:41,759 --> 00:04:44,211
Well done, Buffalo Crush!

107
00:04:44,211 --> 00:04:45,954
Black Hook!

108
00:04:45,954 --> 00:04:48,730
Now. Take the Metal Breath from him!

109
00:04:48,730 --> 00:04:50,100
Jun. Summon me now!

110
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,466
I can't!

111
00:04:51,466 --> 00:04:54,278
If I do that, you'll be found out!

112
00:04:54,278 --> 00:04:57,624
Small fry. I'm giving you 'til the count of three,

113
00:04:57,624 --> 00:05:00,800
to hand over the treasure of planet Machina!

114
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,998
One.

115
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:06,358
What do I do? I can't summon them with my parents here. They'll find out everything!

116
00:05:06,358 --> 00:05:07,661
Two...

117
00:05:07,661 --> 00:05:08,870
I don't have a choice!

118
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:09,254
Three!

119
00:05:09,254 --> 00:05:10,737
No!

120
00:05:12,319 --> 00:05:13,338
Buffalo Crush?...

121
00:05:13,338 --> 00:05:15,819
Told you, me get Machina treasure!

122
00:05:15,819 --> 00:05:18,752
Do promise mean nothing to pirates?

123
00:05:18,752 --> 00:05:23,562
If it means obtaining the Metal Breath, such promises are insignificant.

124
00:05:23,562 --> 00:05:24,300
Jun!

125
00:05:25,677 --> 00:05:28,877
Dad! Mom! I'm sorry! I'll explain everything later!

126
00:05:28,877 --> 00:05:30,466
Jun! What are you doing?!

127
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,935
Metal Breath, pickup!

128
00:05:35,937 --> 00:05:37,545
Shadow X, setup!

129
00:05:38,865 --> 00:05:37,187
!

130
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:43,185
Step aside!

131
00:05:43,185 --> 00:05:44,944
H-he summoned a robot!

132
00:05:44,944 --> 00:05:45,997
Our son did that?!

133
00:05:45,997 --> 00:05:48,358
Shadow X, blow them away with your Heli-Tornado!

134
00:05:48,358 --> 00:05:49,353
Okay!

135
00:05:49,353 --> 00:05:51,528
Heli-Tornado!

136
00:05:51,632 --> 00:05:53,125
Quickly! Lower the sails!

137
00:05:59,151 --> 00:06:01,225
You've made your last move.

138
00:06:01,225 --> 00:06:03,459
Now it's my turn to blow you to smithereens!

139
00:06:03,574 --> 00:06:04,987
Stop!

140
00:06:04,987 --> 00:06:06,355
Me say it again.

141
00:06:06,355 --> 00:06:08,822
You leave this to Buffalo Crush!

142
00:06:15,442 --> 00:06:17,745
Have it your way, then.

143
00:06:17,745 --> 00:06:19,146
Hurry up and take the Metal Breath!

144
00:06:19,146 --> 00:06:21,074
We're leaving, Buster Gallon.

145
00:06:21,074 --> 00:06:23,329
Of cou- Huh?

146
00:06:23,329 --> 00:06:25,555
Where are you going?! Hold on, Black Hook!

147
00:06:25,555 --> 00:06:28,439
That's Captain Black Hook! Captain!!

148
00:06:30,326 --> 00:06:32,415
T-Thank you, Buffalo Crush...

149
00:06:32,415 --> 00:06:33,923
Metal Breath...

150
00:06:33,923 --> 00:06:35,783
is treasure from planet Machina.

151
00:06:35,783 --> 00:06:38,399
It not yours to keep.

152
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:39,319
That's not true.

153
00:06:39,319 --> 00:06:40,358
Blue Cop?

154
00:06:41,927 --> 00:06:43,706
Jun is qualified to have it.

155
00:06:43,706 --> 00:06:47,286
That is why I gave the Metal Breath, entrusted to me by Deus Machina, to Jun.

156
00:06:47,286 --> 00:06:49,694
Qualified? How you know?

157
00:06:49,694 --> 00:06:53,264
The fact that Jun is wearing the Metal Breath... is the proof.

158
00:06:53,264 --> 00:06:57,831
I don't really get it... but it seems like other people can't wear this.

159
00:06:57,831 --> 00:06:59,793
Me don't believe you...

160
00:06:59,793 --> 00:07:01,348
Then how about a fight?

161
00:07:01,348 --> 00:07:02,406
What?

162
00:07:02,406 --> 00:07:06,290
Try to fight him! And you'll find out just how worthy Jun is!

163
00:07:06,290 --> 00:07:08,124
I don't like violence...

164
00:07:08,124 --> 00:07:10,958
but I'm ready to prove my friendship with the Metal Cardbots!

165
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,692
Okay.

166
00:07:16,805 --> 00:07:18,170
We fight!

167
00:07:20,997 --> 00:07:23,711
It's dangerous here. Please come with me.

168
00:07:23,711 --> 00:07:25,143
We're staying with Jun.

169
00:07:25,143 --> 00:07:26,588
We can't leave, we're his parents!

170
00:07:26,588 --> 00:07:28,677
Now, now, this way please!

171
00:07:28,677 --> 00:07:31,470
It's ok! You can watch from where it's safe.

172
00:07:33,581 --> 00:07:35,182
Mega Trucker, setup!

173
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:43,747
Mega Trucker, Mega Power Tackle!

174
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,153
Finally! I was getting bored!

175
00:07:57,365 --> 00:08:00,139
This is awesome! It's a battle of all brawn and no brains!

176
00:08:00,139 --> 00:08:01,689
Wanna say that again?!

177
00:08:11,951 --> 00:08:14,230
Not over yet!

178
00:08:23,141 --> 00:08:24,822
Buffalo Vision!

179
00:08:27,233 --> 00:08:29,403
A laser beam attack?! Not fair!

180
00:08:31,478 --> 00:08:33,239
What is that green stuff?

181
00:08:33,239 --> 00:08:34,389
That's...

182
00:08:36,581 --> 00:08:40,360
Oh dear! It looks like his wound hasn't fully healed yet!

183
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,620
Thank you, Mom!

184
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:45,356
Mega Trucker, Mega Touchdown!

185
00:08:48,927 --> 00:08:52,596
Mega Touchdown!

186
00:08:59,913 --> 00:09:01,293
Let's finish this!

187
00:09:01,585 --> 00:09:03,312
Dexter, setup!

188
00:09:07,195 --> 00:09:08,885
Dexter, into the ground!

189
00:09:12,523 --> 00:09:15,227
Hungry...

190
00:09:15,227 --> 00:09:19,100
Dexter, aim for the Milky Way!

191
00:09:19,610 --> 00:09:21,293
Spiral Ray!

192
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:26,803
Spiral Ray!

193
00:09:40,577 --> 00:09:43,572
Metal Cardbot, Change Up!

194
00:10:02,582 --> 00:10:05,519
Buffalo Crush... sealed!

195
00:10:07,964 --> 00:10:09,702
I hope this proves it for you.

196
00:10:09,702 --> 00:10:11,743
Yahoo! A new subordinate!

197
00:10:11,743 --> 00:10:13,648
Hey, we don't work that way, Shadow X!

198
00:10:13,648 --> 00:10:14,490
Huh?

199
00:10:14,551 --> 00:10:16,480
Are we really just going to leave him?!

200
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,677
He told us to leave it to him!

201
00:10:18,677 --> 00:10:21,148
A pirate does not go back on his word!

202
00:10:21,148 --> 00:10:23,529
Goodbye, Buffalo Crush!

203
00:10:23,529 --> 00:10:25,298
Are you actually crying?

204
00:10:25,298 --> 00:10:26,134
Shut up!

205
00:10:28,495 --> 00:10:29,971
Mom, Dad...

206
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:32,903
I'm sorry I've been hiding this from you guys!

207
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:34,975
You don't have to be sorry.

208
00:10:35,442 --> 00:10:39,956
Jun, we have known about the Metaca... I mean, the Metal Cardbots all along.

209
00:10:39,956 --> 00:10:41,307
It's no surprise.

210
00:10:41,754 --> 00:10:42,941
Eh???

211
00:10:42,941 --> 00:10:47,240
You've been coming home late, your most treasured bike all smashed up...

212
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,740
It was all just too strange.

213
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:53,625
So we confronted Edo. And then asked him to tell us everything he knew!

214
00:10:53,625 --> 00:10:56,533
So... he told us everything that's happened up 'til now.

215
00:10:56,533 --> 00:11:00,211
Uh, there's this robot from the planet Machina called Blue Cop!-

216
00:11:00,211 --> 00:11:02,788
Your mom and dad can see through everything.

217
00:11:02,788 --> 00:11:08,110
And not just that... we know what else you've been hiding.

218
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:09,254
Uh oh...

219
00:11:09,254 --> 00:11:10,760
So... you mean...

220
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:13,307
Do you have anything you want to tell me?

221
00:11:13,307 --> 00:11:16,480
Maybe something like any worries or secrets you may have?

222
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,149
Was this what you were talking about in the car?!

223
00:11:19,149 --> 00:11:21,149
Your scores have been really bad.

224
00:11:21,149 --> 00:11:23,538
But what's worse is hiding them from us.

225
00:11:23,538 --> 00:11:25,288
That makes me really sad.

226
00:11:25,288 --> 00:11:28,620
I-I'm really sorry, Mom and Dad!

